<title>JAPAN: Yaohan Japan falls on loss-cut selling.</title>
<headline>Yaohan Japan falls on loss-cut selling.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yaohan Japan Corp shares fell in Friday afternoon trade as investors launched a fresh round of loss-cut selling, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0510 GMT, the shares were down six yen at 414 yen, on trade of 3.70 million shares, the fifth most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
</text>
